        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran did not try to rebuild enrichment after June 2025 attack, US intel chief says Middle East Issued on: 18/03/2026 - 21:45 Iran made no effort to rebuild uranium enrichment after its capabilities were destroyed in a June 2025 US-Israeli attack, US intelligence chief Tulsi Gabbard testified Wednesday, contradicting President Donald Trump's justifications for his ongoing war. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington. 'Acute risk' that Iraq could become once again victim of internal conflict as Iran war progresses 18/03/2026 Middle East Both sides in Iran war ratchet up attacks on energy facilities, as oil prices surge 18/03/2026 Middle East Elisa Catalano Ewers: Israeli leadership moves to destabilise regime’s leadership structure 18/03/2026 Middle East Soler i Lecha: Foreign policy of Pedro Sánchez 'widely supported by the Spanish population' 18/03/2026 Spain Crowds gather for funeral of top security official Ali Larijani 18/03/2026 Middle East Beirut building collapses amid fresh Israeli strikes in capital city's centre 18/03/2026 Middle East Iran using cluster munitions in retaliatory strikes on Israel 17/03/2026 Middle East Top Iranian officials killed in Israeli airstrike in wartime blow to country's leadership 17/03/2026 Middle East Trump team applying pressure to media: Tell the war's story the way we see it 17/03/2026 Middle East"
